  "step_3": "The decision reason prefers the lottery with the lower probability of the maximum outcome. The individual, however, preferred Lottery B, which has a higher probability (34%) of the maximum outcome, despite the reason favoring the lower one. The individual’s justification was based on a desire to increase the probability of winning by 1%, which directly contradicts the decision reason’s preference for lower probability of the maximum outcome. The individual considered the probabilities of the maximum outcomes and made a choice based on increasing that probability, even though it goes against the rule of the given reason. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason; instead, they used a different rule—preferring higher probability of the maximum outcome. The information considered (probabilities of maximum outcomes) is relevant, but the rule applied is opposite to the decision reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
